==English==
[[File:Domino effect.jpg|thumb|Domino effect]]

===Etymology===
An [[allusion]] to a row of dominoes in which the fall of one leads to a cascade of falling pieces.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The situation in which one [[event]] sets off a [[chain]] of additional events.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Philip Oltermann|title=Switzerland’s national pride dealt heavy blow by the merger of its banking titans|work=The Guardian|date=2023-03-22|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/22/switzerlands-national-pride-dealt-heavy-blow-by-the-merger-of-its-banking-titans|issn=0261-3077|passage=While the move has, for now, calmed fears of a repeat of a 2008-style '''domino effect''', the merger has left Switzerland with a new megabank on Paradeplatz square.}}
# {{lb|en|politics|historical}} The [[theory]] that, if [[South Vietnam]] fell to [[Communism]], it would be followed by [[Cambodia]], [[Laos]], additional [[Southeast Asia|Southeast Asian]] countries, other Asian countries, and likely even elsewhere.
#: {{syn|en|domino theory}}

